<body lang=3D"en-SE" link=3D"blue" vlink=3D"purple" style=3D"word-wrap:brea=
k-word">
<div class=3D"WordSection1">
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">Hi,</span><span lang=3D"EN-US">=
<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">When using X25519MLKEM768, I wo=
uld like to know that the other peer is not reusing its key share (as long =
as it is compliant). As a server reusing a key share can have catastrophic =
security consequences for the client,
 I think this is a _very_ reasonable request.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><a href=3D"https://emanjon.gith=
ub.io/NIST-comments/2025%20-%20SP%20800-227.pdf">https://emanjon.github.io/=
NIST-comments/2025%20-%20SP%20800-227.pdf</a><o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">I don't care about x25519, secp=
256r1, etc., We are planning to support X25519MLKEM768 as soon as possible =
and then disable all groups that are not quantum-resistant as soon as possi=
ble. I also don=92t care about SecP256r1MLKEM768
 and SecP384r1MLKEM1024 as we are not planning to support them.<o:p></o:p><=
/span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">I don't care about what other p=
eople do. If someone want to use (semi-)static keys for performance or visi=
bility, that is fine with me as long as I have the option to not communicat=
e with such implementations.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">I see three solutions:<o:p></o:=
p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">1. Add normative text for X2551=
9MLKEM768, MUST NOT reuse key share.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">2. Add signaling that the key s=
hare is reused so peers have the option to abort the connection (similar to=
 draft-rhrd-tls-tls13-visibility).<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">3. Register two different X2551=
9MLKEM768 groups. One forbidding reuse and one allowing reuse (similar to
</span>TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA vs. TLS_ECDH_ECDSA<span lang=3D"EN-US">).<o:p></o:p>=
</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">I find the current situation of=
 key shares being reused without the other peer knowing inacceptable and fr=
ankly the worst possible option.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">As the old PRs were closed in t=
he hope the issue was already solved and changes to draft-ietf-tls-hybrid-d=
esign does not solve the issue unless normatively referenced form draft-kwi=
atkowski-tls-ecdhe-mlkem, I opened a
 new issue.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><a href=3D"https://github.com/p=
ost-quantum-cryptography/draft-kwiatkowski-tls-ecdhe-mlkem/issues/34">https=
://github.com/post-quantum-cryptography/draft-kwiatkowski-tls-ecdhe-mlkem/i=
ssues/34</a><o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">Cheers,<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">John<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;mso-fareast-language=
:EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"margin-bottom:12.0pt">On 2024-12-25, 07:08,=
 &quot;internet-drafts@ietf.org&quot; &lt;internet-drafts@ietf.org&gt; wrot=
e:<o:p></o:p></p>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">Internet-Draft draft-kwiatkowski-tls-ecdhe-mlkem-03.=
txt is now available.<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;&nbsp; Title:&nbsp;&nbsp; Post-quantum hybrid =
ECDHE-MLKEM Key Agreement for TLSv1.3<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;&nbsp; Authors: Kris Kwiatkowski<o:p></o:p></p=
>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbs=
p;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Panos Kampanakis<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbs=
p;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Bas Westerbaan<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbs=
p;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Douglas Stebila<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;&nbsp; Name:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;draft-kwia=
tkowski-tls-ecdhe-mlkem-03.txt<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;&nbsp; Pages:&nbsp;&nbsp; 9<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;&nbsp; Dates:&nbsp;&nbsp; 2024-12-24<o:p></o:p=
></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">Abstract:<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;&nbsp; This draft defines three hybrid key agr=
eements for TLS 1.3:<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;&nbsp; X25519MLKEM768, SecP256r1MLKEM768, and =
SecP384r1MLKEM1024 which<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;&nbsp; combine a post-quantum KEM with an elli=
ptic curve Diffie-Hellman<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;&nbsp; (ECDHE).<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">The IETF datatracker status page for this Internet-D=
raft is:<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><a href=3D"https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-kw=
iatkowski-tls-ecdhe-mlkem/">https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-kwiatkow=
ski-tls-ecdhe-mlkem/</a><o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>
</div>
